   $ cd $HOME/work/a3/run5
1. The public configuration: the parameter file, the scales, the layout of a proof's arrays
   $ cp $HOME/work/flashprove-sm120/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/policy.txt $HOME/work/flashprove-sm120/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/KL.bin $HOME/work/flashprove-sm120/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/layout.txt config/
2. cp_commit draws a seed and commits to the weights: ivk/ is for the clients, isk/ stays with the provider
   $ /usr/bin/time -v $HOME/work/a3/progs/cp_commit -weights made-up-blocks -config config -M 1 -ivk ivk -isk isk > cp_commit.log 2>&1
   the commitment's ID, to be published: cf1eb68b9594a1bebe831769303e4ad4b5c1a93b01c821291a063e46f102e5a9
3. The request: a made-up prompt, the model's own first choices after it, and the question whether each of them is that, and which token comes next
   $ cp $HOME/work/flashprove-sm120/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/own_choices.req in/example.req
4. cp_prove runs the model on the request and writes the answer and its proof
   $ /usr/bin/time -v env HOME=$HOME/work/a3/run5/home TMPDIR=$HOME/work/a3/run5/tmp $HOME/work/a3/progs/cp_prove -isk $HOME/work/a3/run5/isk -in $HOME/work/a3/run5/in -out $HOME/work/a3/run5/out > cp_prove.log 2>&1
